    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d178">

                <pb facs="0189" n="867" sameAs="frus:frus1863p2/pg867"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr. Clay.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 8.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1863-05-11"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >May</hi> 11, 1863.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I think it proper that you should be
                    possessed of a copy of a note which I have this day addressed to Mr. Dayton, in
                    regard to a suggestion that this government should concur with the governments
                    of France, Austria, and Great Britain, in presenting their views of the
                    insurrection in Poland to the consideration of the Emperor of Russia.</p>
                <p>There can be no impropriety in your informally making known the contents of the
                    paper to Prince Gortchacow.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Cassius</hi> M. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Clay</hi>, Esq., <hi rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c.,
                        &amp;c.</hi></p>
                    <p>Same to Mr. Adams, No. 591.</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
